      article.main
        h1 Code
        p Pug allows you to write inline JavaScript code in your templates. There are three types of code: Unbuffered, Buffered, and Unescaped Buffered.
        h2#unbuffered-code
          | Unbuffered Code
          a.header-anchor(href="#unbuffered-code", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p
          | Unbuffered code starts with
          code -
          | . It does not directly add anything to the output.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="0")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="-1891989992")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  - for (var x = 0; x < 3; x++)
                    li item
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <li>item</li>
                  <li>item</li>
                  <li>item</li>
        p Pug also supports block unbuffered code:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="1")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="1224788240")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  -
                    var list = ["Uno", "Dos", "Tres",
                            "Cuatro", "Cinco", "Seis"]
                  each item in list
                    li= item
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <li>Uno</li>
                  <li>Dos</li>
                  <li>Tres</li>
                  <li>Cuatro</li>
                  <li>Cinco</li>
                  <li>Seis</li>
        h2#buffered-code
          | Buffered Code
          a.header-anchor(href="#buffered-code", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p
          | Buffered code starts with
          code =
          | . It evaluates the JavaScript expression and outputs the result. For security, buffered code is first HTML escaped.
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="2")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="928743917")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  p
                    = 'This code is <escaped>!'
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <p>This code is &lt;escaped&gt;!</p>
        p It can also be written inline (after any attributes), and supports the full range of JavaScript expressions:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="3")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="-1152334203")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  p= 'This code is' + ' <escaped>!'
                  p(style="background: blue")= 'A message with a ' + 'blue' + ' background'
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <p>This code is &lt;escaped&gt;!</p>
                  <p style="background: blue">A message with a blue background</p>
        h2#unescaped-buffered-code
          | Unescaped Buffered Code
          a.header-anchor(href="#unescaped-buffered-code", aria-hidden="true") ¶
        p
          | Unescaped buffered code starts with
          code !=
          | . It evaluates the JavaScript expression and outputs the result. Unescaped buffered code does not perform any escaping, so is unsafe for user input:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="4")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="1050186186")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  p
                    != 'This code is <strong>not</strong> escaped!'
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <p>This code is <strong>not</strong> escaped!</p>
        p Unescaped buffered code can also be written inline with attributes, and supports the full range of JavaScript expressions:
        div.preview-wrapper(data-control="interactive", data-index="5")
          div.row(data-reactroot, data-reactid="1", data-react-checksum="-17460043")
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="2")
              div(data-reactid="3")
                textarea(data-reactid="4").
                  p!= 'This code is' + ' <strong>not</strong> escaped!'
            div.col-lg-6(data-reactid="5")
              div(data-reactid="6")
                textarea(readonly, data-reactid="7").
                  <p>This code is <strong>not</strong> escaped!</p>
        div.alert.alert-danger
          h6 Caution
          p
            strong Unescaped buffered code can be dangerous.
            | You must be sure to sanitize any user inputs to avoid
            a(href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross-site_scripting") cross-site scripting
            | (XSS).
        div(style="margin-top: 50px")
          div.AW-Form-692213006
